From 8b2a15d9a5fa4a968d20a83797e94469e7e9a375 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nmcintosh <nathanielstewartmcintosh@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 23:06:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] launcher: OmacVM's Mac side for the guest's org.omacvm.*
 agents, full screen over the notch

Ports org.omacvm.battery, org.omacvm.media, org.omacvm.camera and org.omacvm.auth
(libkrun virtio-console ports on a socketpair) with OmacVM.app's bridges ported from
github.com/gillesgoetsch/omacvm (MIT): the Mac's battery, AirPods/Now Playing media
controls, the camera (NV12 frames on demand) and the Touch ID relay to OmacVM Bridge.
Protocols unchanged. Each one can be left out: --no-omacvm-battery, --no-omacvm-media,
--no-omacvm-camera, --no-touchid.

FullPanel: on a MacBook with a notch, a boot that opens full screen on the built-in
display covers the whole panel (AppKit's menu bar reservation answered no for the VM
window, the menu bar backdrop transparent, menu bar and Dock held back) and the guest
gets omacvm.fullpanel=LxRxHxWxD on its command line. --no-fullpanel turns it off.
